#!/bin/sh
set -e
# Stop a running console so dpkg can replace binaries. Needed when upgrading
# from packages whose prerm did not stop the unit on "upgrade".
if [ "$1" = "upgrade" ] || [ "$1" = "install" ]; then
  if command -v systemctl >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    systemctl stop privgate.service 2>/dev/null || true
  fi
  # A console started by hand is not managed by systemd. Ask it to drain
  # gracefully (SIGTERM), wait briefly, force only as a last resort.
  if command -v pgrep >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    PIDS="$(pgrep -f '/opt/privgate/bin/node /opt/privgate/host.cjs' 2>/dev/null || true)"
    if [ -n "$PIDS" ]; then
      kill -TERM $PIDS 2>/dev/null || true
      i=0
      while [ "$i" -lt 8 ]; do
        pgrep -f '/opt/privgate/bin/node /opt/privgate/host.cjs' >/dev/null 2>&1 || break
        sleep 1
        i=$((i + 1))
      done
      if pgrep -f '/opt/privgate/bin/node /opt/privgate/host.cjs' >/dev/null 2>&1; then
        kill -KILL $PIDS 2>/dev/null || true
        sleep 1
      fi
    fi
  fi
fi
